11. Recommended learning order
Follow this sequence rather than learning all topics at once.
8-week study plan
0 of 7 completed

Weeks 1–2
SQL fundamentals
Filtering, joins, aggregations, CTEs, subqueries and window functions

Week 3
Databricks fundamentals
Workspace, notebooks, compute, SQL warehouses and Catalog Explorer

Week 4
Python and PySpark
DataFrames, transformations, joins, cleaning and aggregation

Week 5
Delta Lake and data modelling
Delta tables, medallion architecture, fact and dimension tables

Week 6
Databricks SQL and dashboards
Queries, KPIs, visualizations and Power BI integration

Week 7
ETL and workflows
Data ingestion, incremental loads, jobs, quality checks and monitoring

Week 8
Project and interview preparation
Complete one end-to-end project and practise SQL interview questions
Suggested pace: 1–2 hours daily. Adjust the schedule based on your current SQL and Python skills.
